/-!
# Certified elements of an M23 involution centralizer

Seven explicit permutations preserve the 253 heptads and commute with the
representative. The first four fix its heptad pointwise; the last three provide
candidates for the induced Fano-plane action. The table inverses, block actions,
and commutation identities are all checked by Lean's kernel.

These are concrete inputs to the lower bound for the centralizer in
Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, Lemma 5.2.21,
printed p.657 (PDF p.674). The tables were found by permutation calculations;
no external group-order calculation is used as a proof.
-/

